course: dictionary
lesson: 16015
title: Words for choices and beliefs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Vegetarianism is easy to break into parts. Vegetarian describes someone who does not eat meat or fish, and the ending -ism means a practice or a way of living. So vegetarianism is the practice of not eating meat or fish.
explain: Look at the context clues. «Mia practises vegetarianism because she cares about animals.» The word because tells you the reason, and caring about animals is a reason for not eating meat, so vegetarianism must be the practice of not eating meat.
explain: «Our family switched to vegetarianism last year to help the planet.» Switched tells you the family changed how they eat, and to help the planet tells you why. Swap your meaning into the sentence: the practice of not eating meat or fish fits perfectly, so your meaning works.
fact: Vegetarianism is the practice of not eating meat or fish.
fact: «Vegetarianism» is a noun, and it is uncountable, so you do not add an s to it.
fact: People follow vegetarianism for many reasons: for animals, for their health, for the planet, or because of their faith or family.
fact: A person who follows vegetarianism is called a vegetarian.
fact: Phrases to know: «practise vegetarianism» (to follow it) and «switch to vegetarianism» (to start following it).
exercise: «Mia practises vegetarianism because she cares about animals.» What is vegetarianism? | *The practice of not eating meat or fish | A sport played with a ball | Eating only sweets | A type of fast food
exercise: «Our family switched to vegetarianism last year.» Find and copy one word that shows they changed how they eat. | family | year | *switched | last
exercise: Which is a reason someone might choose vegetarianism? | *To care for animals | To win a race | To get out of school | To grow taller by eating more sweets
test: Lena's family follows vegetarianism for their faith. What does follow vegetarianism mean? | To buy new clothes | *To keep to the practice of not eating meat or fish | To eat meat only on Sundays | To cook dinner for guests
test: Which word names the practice itself, not a person? | vegetarian | *vegetarianism | vegetable | meat
exam: Which sentence uses vegetarianism correctly? | She vegetarianism the apple pie at lunch. | Vegetarianism ran very quickly around the track. | *The class learned that vegetarianism means not eating meat or fish.
